From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 12:05:15 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat(visu): optional icon size for the Link widget

The Link widget always rendered its icon at text-4xl, and VisuIcon
fits every SVG into a 1em square, so a wide SVG (e.g. a 393x207 car
picture) shrank to a thin strip in the middle of the tile.

Add an optional icon_size config value (px). 0 or a missing/invalid
value keeps the previous rendering (text-4xl, 1em square), so existing
widgets are unchanged. With a size set, the icon wrapper spans the tile
and uses that font size; VisuIcon gets an opt-in fitWidth prop that
renders the SVG 1em high with automatic width, capped at the container
width, so the aspect ratio is kept. Emoji just scale with the font size.
All other VisuIcon callers keep the 1em square.

The Link config panel gets a numeric input with de/en strings, the
widget default config gains icon_size: 0, and vitests cover the default,
the fallback for invalid values, the custom size and the SVG sizing.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
